    {
      "_why_two_modules_components": [
        "The design's §5, measured off the owner's own three A1200 Kickstarts:",
        "a 3.2 ROM (header 47.96, exec 47.7, strap 45.1) gets modules on with the",
        "larger set, a 3.2.1 ROM (47.102, exec 47.8, strap 47.2) gets modules on",
        "with the smaller set, and a 3.2.2 ROM (47.111, exec 47.10, strap 47.2)",
        "gets modules off. `exec_rev < 10` alone tells 3.2.2 apart from the other",
        "two; `strap < 47` alone tells 3.2 apart from 3.2.1 — no `and`/`or` needed.",
        "",
        "Measured with `xdftool ModulesA1200_3.2.2.adf list`: the disk carries",
        "exactly one machine drawer, `LIBS/A1200/exec.library`; `LIBS/intuition.library`,",
        "`L/{Ram-Handler,Shell-Seg,System-startup}` and",
        "`LIBS/{dos,gadtools,graphics}.library` are all present too.",
        "`DEVS/A1200/scsi.device`, `L/FastFileSystem`, `LIBS/Modules/` and",
        "`LIBS/Resources/` are on the disk and the 3.2.2 installer never copies",
        "them — a rule for any of them would be ART installing something the",
        "release does not."
      ],
      "_why_overrides_modules_a1200": [
        "Final whole-branch review, Finding B. `exclusive_group: \"modules\"`",
        "was copied onto this component from the base `modules-a1200`'s shape",
        "without asking whether the group still meant the same thing once both",
        "could be on at once — a pre-47 Kickstart satisfies both this",
        "component's own condition (`exec < 47.10`) and the base layer's",
        "(`rom-older-than 47`) at the same time, which is the ordinary case for",
        "the real Amigas this project exists for, not an edge case. They are",
        "not a user's choice between two machines (what the group exists to",
        "police); they are two halves of one release's answer for one",
        "machine, so `plan::detect_exclusive_group_conflicts` now scopes the",
        "group per layer and does not refuse this pair. What is still real:",
        "both components' rules name `LIBS/A1200` as a `Subtree`, so declaring",
        "the override here is what lets this update's own newer files in that",
        "drawer win over the base's, the same shape `update-322-diskdoctor`",
        "and `workbench-39` already use for a genuine two-layer overlap."
      ],
      "id": "update-322-modules-a1200",
      "media": "ModulesA1200_3.2.2",
      "layer": "update-3.2.2",
      "exclusive_group": "modules",
      "label_key": "osinstall.components.name.os322.modulesA1200",
      "condition": {
        "condition": "resident-older-than",
        "resident": "exec",
        "major": 47,
        "minor": 10
      },
      "overrides": ["modules-a1200", "storage", "workbench-base"],
      "rules": [
        { "from": "LIBS/A1200", "to": "Libs/A1200", "kind": "subtree" },
        { "from": "LIBS/intuition.library", "to": "Libs/intuition.library", "kind": "file" },
        { "from": "L/Ram-Handler", "to": "L/Ram-Handler", "kind": "file" },
        { "from": "L/System-startup", "to": "L/System-startup", "kind": "file" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "update-322-modules-a1200-strap",
      "media": "ModulesA1200_3.2.2",
      "layer": "update-3.2.2",
      "label_key": "osinstall.components.name.os322.modulesA1200Strap",
      "condition": {
        "condition": "resident-older-than",
        "resident": "strap",
        "major": 47
      },
      "overrides": ["update-322-modules-a1200", "workbench-base"],
      "rules": [
        { "from": "L/Shell-Seg", "to": "L/Shell-Seg", "kind": "file" },
        { "from": "L/Ram-Handler", "to": "L/Ram-Handler", "kind": "file" },
        { "from": "L/System-startup", "to": "L/System-startup", "kind": "file" },
        { "from": "LIBS/dos.library", "to": "Libs/dos.library", "kind": "file" },
        { "from": "LIBS/gadtools.library", "to": "Libs/gadtools.library", "kind": "file" },
        { "from": "LIBS/graphics.library", "to": "Libs/graphics.library", "kind": "file" }
      ]
    }
